{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent legal battles that ensued. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his quick-witted dialogue and complex characters.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. he is a brilliant computer programmer, but he is also socially awkward and struggles to connect with others. after a painful breakup with his girlfriend, erica, mark creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes a huge success, but it also gets mark into trouble with the university administration. he is then approached by a group of students, including twins cameron and tyler winklevoss, who ask him to create a social networking site for harvard students. mark agrees, but he soon becomes obsessed with the project and begins to work on it himself, with the help of his friend eduardo saverin.\n\nas the site grows in popularity, mark and eduardo become wealthy and famous, but they also attract the attention of the winklevoss twins, who claim that mark stole their idea. the twins sue mark and facebook, and the film follows the subsequent legal battles, as well as the personal struggles of the characters.\n\nthe film features a talented cast, including andrew garfield as eduardo saverin and justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder of napster. the performances are all excellent, with eisenberg standing out as the complex and nuanced mark zuckerberg.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy. it is a dark and moody soundtrack that perfectly captures the tone of the film. the cinematography, handled by jeff cronenweth, is also excellent, with a muted color palette that reflects the cold and calculating world of the characters.\n\none of the strengths of the film is its ability to balance the technical aspects of the story with the personal struggles of the characters. the film does a great job of explaining the creation of facebook and the subsequent legal battles, but it also delves deep into the personalities and motivations of the characters.\n\noverall, the social network is a fascinating and engaging film that explores the complexities of the digital age. it is a film that will resonate with anyone who has ever used facebook or any other social networking site, and it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of mark zuckerberg and the founding of facebook.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028338772244751453}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0297507643699646}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.005243951920419931}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.4364714026451111}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00035589560866355896}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.4011722505092621}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.009412200190126896}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.02339894324541092}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00021300431399140507}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.2014133334159851}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.5591464042663574}, {"token": " legal", "logprob": -0.9605181813240051}, {"token": " battles", "logprob": -0.0008984343148767948}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0002469711471349001}, {"token": " ensued", "logprob": -0.35183119773864746}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -1.4185804502631072e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.001